<div class="span9 about-main-image">
<div class="span6 about-description"><h1>HPD Design Guidelines for New Construction</h1>
<div class="img-right-vert"><a href="/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/hpd-design-guidelines-for-new-construction-2026.pdf"> <img style="border: 1px solid #ccc;" src="/assets/hpd/images/content/pages/hpd-design-guidelines-for-new-construction-2026.jpg" alt="HPD Design Guidelines cover page." /> </a></div>
<p>The <a href="/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/hpd-design-guidelines-for-new-construction-2026.pdf" title="HPD Design Guidelines for New Construction 2026"><strong>HPD Design Guidelines for New Construction 2026</strong></a> (the "Guidelines"), released in July of 2026, establish the design and building performance criteria by which HPD evaluates proposed developments for multifamily new construction, supportive, and senior housing projects.</p>
<p>HPD seeks to support projects that meet several core principles. Projects should:</p>
<ul>
<li>Have a strong relation to the neighborhood (urban design and building planning)</li>
<li>Meet the needs of households and individuals (apartment planning and accessible design)</li>
<li>Promote greater equity</li>
<li>Encourage active design and better health outcomes</li>
<li>Minimize climate impact and enhance climate resiliency</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Applicability</strong></p>
<p>Design acceptance by HPD&rsquo;s Office of Development&rsquo;s Division of Building and Land Development Services (BLDS) is a prerequisite to loan closing for new construction projects developed under HPD loan subsidy programs.</p>
<p>The 2026 release of the Guidelines for New Construction apply to projects submitted for Design Consultation on or after <strong>October 1, 2026.</strong></p>
<p><em>Note:</em> Projects participating solely in <a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/inclusionary-housing.page">Inclusionary Housing incentive programs</a> (Mandatory Inclusionary Housing, Voluntary Inclusionary Housing, or Universal Affordability Preference) that are not subsidized through other HPD loan programs are not subject to the Guidelines but are subject to BLDS review of zoning and accessibility requirements.</p>
<p>All new construction projects subject to the Guidelines are also required to certify with the current version of the NYC Overlay of Enterprise Green Communities (EGC) or LEED Gold or above, in accordance with NYC green building standards established under Local Laws 31 and 32 of 2016 (Capital Green Building Program). Refer to <a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/enterprise-green-communities-criteria-egcc.page">HPD's Green Building Certification webpage</a>.</p>
<p>The design standards established in the Guidelines shall not supersede any legal or statutory design requirements (e.g. New York City Building Code, Zoning Resolution, etc.), and all HPD construction projects remain subject to plan review by the Department of Buildings.</p>
<p><strong>See the detailed guide on the New Construction Design Review Process linked below for more information.</strong></p>
<p><br /></p>
<p><em>For access to the 2023 version of the Guidelines, please see <a href="/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/hpd-design-guidelines-for-new-construction-2023.pdf">here</a>. To access the corresponding Workbook, please see <a href="/assets/hpd/downloads/excel/NC-design-guidelines-workbook_2023.xlsx">here</a>.</em></p>
<p><strong>Design Review Process &amp; Submission Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/new-construction-design-review-process-guide.pdf">New Construction Design Review Process Guide</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/assets/hpd/downloads/excel/NC-design-guidelines-workbook.xlsx">New Construction Design Guidelines Workbook</a> (<em>*Updated*</em>)</li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/hpd-blds-new-construction-design-consultation-submission-checklist.pdf">Design Consultation Submission Checklist</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/hpd-blds-new-construction-design-review-submission-checklist.pdf">Design Review Submission Checklist</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/hpd-blds-nc-precon-accessibility-statement.pdf">Pre-Construction Accessibility Statement</a></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Additional Resources</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/nc-design-guidelines-faq.pdf">Design Guidelines FAQ</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/hpd-sustainability-technical-requirements.page">Technical Requirements</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/hpd-heating-policy.page">HPD&rsquo;s Electric Heating Policy</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/underwriting-electric-high-performance-buildings.page">HPD&rsquo;s Underwriting Electric and High Performance Buildings Webpage</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/clarifications-on-electric-resistance-nc.pdf">Clarifications on Electric Resistance</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/memo-uswr-rooftop-conflicts.pdf">Guidance on Unified Stormwater Rule Compliance and Rooftop Conflicts</a></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Presentations &amp; Trainings</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/assets/hpd/downloads/pdfs/services/hpd-new-construction-design-guidelines-training-presentation.pdf">HPD Design Guidelines for New Construction 2026: What's New</a></li>
<li><a href="https://youtu.be/3QkeVJ-YRm0">Introducing the HPD Design Guidelines for New Construction 2026 Video Recording</a></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Additional Information &amp; Contacts</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/new-construction-financing.page">New Construction</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/blds.page">Building and Land Development Services (BLDS)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/sustainability.page">Sustainability</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/resiliency.page">Resiliency</a></li>
</ul></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
